WEBVTT

00:00.021 --> 00:01.189
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION. UNDERAGE
DRINKING IS STRONGLY PROHIBITED.

00:01.189 --> 00:02.482
FORCEFUL ALCOHOL CONSUMPTION, BINGE
DRINKING, SHAMEFUL ACTS NOT ENCOURAGED.

00:02.482 --> 00:03.775
VIEW THIS AS A COMEDY. ALL CHARACTERS
APPEARING IN THIS WORK ARE OF LEGAL AGE.

00:03.775 --> 00:04.984
DUE TO RECENT COMPLIANCE ISSUES, THE
BLACK DOT SIZE HAS BEEN INCREASED BY 5%.

00:16.120 --> 00:18.581
Let's go take a trip
under the bright summer sun

00:18.581 --> 00:21.793
GRAND BLUE DREAMING SEASON 3
To a city far away, what do you say?

00:21.793 --> 00:24.212
Let's go take a trip
under the bright summer sun

00:24.212 --> 00:27.757
To a city far away, what do you say?

00:31.844 --> 00:33.721
Wait a sec, another heatwave?

00:33.721 --> 00:35.431
Temperatures are rising... Huh?!

00:35.431 --> 00:38.643
Our original plans are
totally busted, what now?

00:38.643 --> 00:41.479
But honestly, I'm getting so hyped

00:41.479 --> 00:44.148
Alright, let's roll up
our sleeves and dive in

00:44.148 --> 00:45.900
Rub your sleepy eyes and jump up

00:45.900 --> 00:47.360
Grab the usual shades

00:47.360 --> 00:50.280
Check your gear: Iced coffee, thermos

00:50.280 --> 00:52.949
Clear blue skies, just a trick of summer

00:52.949 --> 00:56.077
The booming speakers
keep calling my name

00:56.411 --> 00:58.913
Even now, I still believe

01:01.833 --> 01:03.793
In unexpected encounters

01:03.793 --> 01:06.379
And the miracles of this season

01:06.379 --> 01:09.632
Summer brings
those swing swing emotions

01:09.632 --> 01:12.385
Ah, even if I get a little carried away

01:12.385 --> 01:17.599
On my mind,
I've only been searching for you

01:17.599 --> 01:23.521
Let the south wind blow you here,
just as you are

01:23.521 --> 01:28.234
Under the blue sky, hold me tight

01:29.068 --> 01:34.490
I want to dream
a summer dream with you

01:35.825 --> 01:38.286
Tomorrow's the last day of
our part-time job, right?

01:38.703 --> 01:40.663
It went by in a flash.

01:41.623 --> 01:43.124
They're back.

01:43.541 --> 01:44.917
Let's go greet them.

01:45.877 --> 01:48.254
I wonder if she's doing okay.

01:50.590 --> 01:53.551
The step down is very slippery.
Please be careful.

01:55.678 --> 01:57.764
It's dangerous to step down from there.

01:57.972 --> 02:00.141
What? It's fine, it's fine.

02:00.350 --> 02:02.894
Only amateurs would fall
from something like this.

02:03.061 --> 02:04.896
But it's still very dangerous.

02:04.979 --> 02:06.481
Please use that way.

02:06.731 --> 02:07.190
Huh?

02:07.607 --> 02:09.776
Are you treating me like
some frail old man?

02:09.984 --> 02:11.235
No, it's not that.

02:11.527 --> 02:14.572
But that spot is especially
slippery and dangerous...

02:14.572 --> 02:16.032
I already know that!

02:16.282 --> 02:19.118
I have ten times the
diving experience you kids have.

02:19.661 --> 02:23.331
And yet, you're nagging so much
about
just
stepping down?

02:23.665 --> 02:26.250
Don't act so high and mighty,
you greenhorns!

02:27.585 --> 02:31.214
So because you're a veteran,
you don't need to care about safety?

02:31.214 --> 02:32.006
Huh?

02:32.131 --> 02:35.468
Complacency from being used
to it is the most fatal thing!

02:35.510 --> 02:36.803
What did you say?

02:36.803 --> 02:37.970
Now, now.

02:38.096 --> 02:40.306
Sorry for nagging you.

02:40.515 --> 02:41.015
Huh?

02:41.391 --> 02:44.018
One look and anyone can tell
you're a pro.

02:44.143 --> 02:44.727
Oh.

02:44.894 --> 02:46.187
That's exactly why.

02:46.354 --> 02:49.440
Amateurs always try to copy
what the pros are doing.

02:49.732 --> 02:50.400
Oh.

02:50.817 --> 02:54.570
It would be troublesome
if beginners tried to copy you.

02:54.737 --> 02:56.572
Well, that makes sense.

02:56.948 --> 02:57.990
So be it.

02:58.324 --> 02:59.492
Thank you.

02:59.742 --> 03:00.159
Yeah.

03:02.578 --> 03:03.788
Iori, great job.

03:03.996 --> 03:05.331
That was impressive.

03:06.582 --> 03:08.459
You're suited for this job.

03:08.626 --> 03:10.294
I don't even know how to swim.

03:10.545 --> 03:13.047
But your personality fits.

03:13.506 --> 03:16.843
You sure can handle people and
you also deal with complaints well.

03:17.176 --> 03:19.011
You won't graduate college anyway.

03:19.011 --> 03:21.889
Give me six years and I'll graduate!

03:25.143 --> 03:26.811
Alright, good job today, everyone.

03:27.186 --> 03:29.397
How about we all go out to eat today?

03:29.522 --> 03:31.441
We haven't had a welcome party anyway.

03:31.983 --> 03:34.569
Tomorrow is the last day
of our part-time job.

03:34.777 --> 03:37.488
Then it'll double as a farewell party.

03:37.780 --> 03:39.782
Sounds good, let's go eat.

03:40.074 --> 03:41.868
Do you guys have any plans?

03:42.326 --> 03:43.911
Of course not.

03:50.168 --> 03:51.878
So delicious!

03:52.128 --> 03:53.671
It's really good.

03:53.671 --> 03:54.839
Right?

03:55.381 --> 03:57.133
Chisa, does your stomach hurt?

03:57.175 --> 03:59.135
Ah, no, I'm fine.

03:59.135 --> 04:01.304
Are you really okay?
Be careful.

04:02.388 --> 04:04.891
How do you guys feel about this job?

04:05.308 --> 04:06.434
Let's see...

04:06.684 --> 04:09.353
The physical labor
is harder than I thought.

04:10.021 --> 04:12.774
As for me, I find dealing
with customers more exhausting.

04:13.024 --> 04:15.109
You barely even deal with them.

04:16.903 --> 04:19.947
When I first started,
I struggled with a lot of things too.

04:20.531 --> 04:22.492
So everyone goes through it.

04:22.909 --> 04:24.994
What do you find
the most difficult now?

04:25.286 --> 04:26.412
Hmm...

04:27.371 --> 04:30.124
Probably having to smile all the time.

04:30.458 --> 04:31.501
Huh?

04:31.501 --> 04:32.376
That's a surprise.

04:32.502 --> 04:33.127
Really?

04:33.127 --> 04:35.546
Because you always seem to be smiling.

04:36.547 --> 04:38.800
I have to put in a lot of effort
to be like that.

04:38.966 --> 04:43.262
But in the end, we are only human,
sometimes it's hard to force a smile.

04:43.846 --> 04:48.142
For the customers,
a day here is going to be special.

04:48.976 --> 04:49.894
You're right.

04:50.394 --> 04:51.729
But for us,

04:51.729 --> 04:54.065
it's just a scene from our daily lives.

04:54.440 --> 04:58.861
There are days when we feel sick,
or are in a bad mood.

04:59.153 --> 05:02.073
At times like that,
it's really hard to smile.

05:02.573 --> 05:03.908
I see.

05:04.283 --> 05:07.328
Chisa, if you did this job,
you'd probably have a hard time.

05:08.579 --> 05:10.248
Excuse me, do you think I am...

05:11.249 --> 05:13.292
not suited for this job?

05:13.626 --> 05:15.378
Uh... About that...

05:15.419 --> 05:17.338
It also depends on your working style.

05:17.588 --> 05:18.881
You're not suited for it.

05:19.757 --> 05:20.842
Boss...

05:21.008 --> 05:24.011
You simply just love the sea and diving.

05:24.720 --> 05:27.056
You're clumsy and not very friendly.

05:27.265 --> 05:29.600
You'll just bring more trouble
upon yourself.

05:29.642 --> 05:33.020
You'd be better off finding a normal job
and keeping diving as a hobby.

05:33.354 --> 05:34.313
I'm not...

05:36.232 --> 05:38.150
I'm not asking you!

05:41.320 --> 05:42.321
Sorry everyone.

05:50.788 --> 05:53.624
Kotegawa looked
absolutely pissed just now.

05:54.584 --> 05:56.669
Kitahara, you know what happened?

05:57.044 --> 05:58.337
No, beats me.

05:58.838 --> 06:02.383
The auntie's just like that,
so they were bound to clash eventually.

06:02.508 --> 06:03.801
True.

06:06.012 --> 06:09.599
It seems my mom doesn't want me
to be a diving instructor.

06:10.182 --> 06:11.601
What's wrong, Cakey?

06:12.059 --> 06:13.811
Oh, nothing.

06:14.270 --> 06:17.148
I should probably ask her
about it tomorrow.

06:17.690 --> 06:18.441
See ya.

06:18.774 --> 06:19.567
Yeah.

06:19.567 --> 06:20.693
Good night.

06:27.408 --> 06:28.451
Is this really okay?

06:28.826 --> 06:29.493
Huh?

06:29.952 --> 06:30.912
What is?

06:31.412 --> 06:34.457
We're only staying in Palau
until tomorrow night.

06:35.166 --> 06:38.044
Don't you have
your own objective to fulfill?

06:39.128 --> 06:41.172
There's no such thing.

06:41.464 --> 06:43.007
Never mind then.

06:43.716 --> 06:45.801
But idling around with your mouth open

06:45.801 --> 06:47.803
won't magically make
the prey fall into it.

06:48.304 --> 06:50.222
Are you trying to act high and mighty?

06:50.222 --> 06:52.934
I'm a veteran in dating sims, you know.

06:53.351 --> 06:56.062
Hmph, I'm going to sleep.

06:57.063 --> 06:58.898
Yeah, good night.

07:03.402 --> 07:04.487
Seriously.

07:05.071 --> 07:06.697
It's really tough...

07:06.906 --> 07:09.241
being the best friend type
in dating sims.

07:16.999 --> 07:17.792
How is it?

07:18.042 --> 07:19.418
No good.

07:19.627 --> 07:21.712
She'll cheer up once we go diving.

07:21.712 --> 07:23.339
I hope so.

07:23.714 --> 07:26.092
Today's group of customers canceled.

07:26.300 --> 07:26.926
Huh?

07:27.301 --> 07:29.178
I heard they got food poisoning.

07:29.428 --> 07:30.262
Oh man.

07:30.262 --> 07:32.014
That's really unlucky.

07:32.014 --> 07:34.141
So we're calling it off today?

07:34.350 --> 07:36.435
We just need to put away
the equipment, right?

07:36.435 --> 07:38.521
We went through everything to ready it.

07:38.521 --> 07:40.106
No complaining.

07:40.314 --> 07:42.483
Wait, I have an idea.

07:49.115 --> 07:50.658
Is this really okay?

07:50.658 --> 07:53.119
Having breaks during work
to go diving like this.

07:53.661 --> 07:55.746
We did go through
the trouble of preparing.

07:55.997 --> 07:58.708
Besides, you three have
only dived on the first day.

07:58.833 --> 08:01.460
It'd be a shame to come to Palau
and only dive once.

08:01.502 --> 08:03.170
- Thank you!
- Thank you!

08:04.130 --> 08:05.548
Aren't you glad, Chisa?

08:05.965 --> 08:07.174
I'm fine either way.

08:07.341 --> 08:08.968
I dive every day anyway.

08:09.051 --> 08:11.012
But that's diving for work.

08:11.178 --> 08:13.681
Diving for fun with friends
is very different.

08:14.223 --> 08:14.974
But...

08:15.099 --> 08:16.684
That's right, Chisa.

08:17.101 --> 08:20.438
Besides, if this keeps up,
your memories of Palau

08:20.438 --> 08:22.231
will be about "
that
place bursting."

08:22.356 --> 08:23.941
Absolutely not!

08:24.400 --> 08:25.317
In that case,

08:25.651 --> 08:28.738
let's make some wonderful memories
so coming here wasn't a waste.

08:39.290 --> 08:41.709
The scenery is as breathtaking as ever.

08:54.472 --> 08:56.432
TRY LYING FACE DOWN

09:01.979 --> 09:03.981
SPOTTED GARDEN EELS
AND SPLENDID GARDEN EELS

09:05.941 --> 09:07.943
CUTE, RIGHT?

09:47.399 --> 09:48.025
So...

09:48.442 --> 09:49.693
amazing!

09:49.693 --> 09:51.278
So those are manta rays?

09:51.278 --> 09:53.114
I didn't expect them to be so huge!

09:53.114 --> 09:55.116
They look really impressive!

09:55.116 --> 09:57.243
Did you see them a lot while working?

09:57.576 --> 09:58.410
No.

09:58.911 --> 10:00.663
It's my first time
seeing them this close.

10:00.871 --> 10:02.331
I see, I see.

10:02.331 --> 10:04.542
In other words, we hit the jackpot!

10:04.542 --> 10:06.043
We're really lucky.

10:06.210 --> 10:06.961
Yeah.

10:07.336 --> 10:10.631
Diving is truly amazing!

10:10.714 --> 10:11.298
Yeah.

10:11.298 --> 10:12.216
Exactly.

10:21.475 --> 10:22.935
I think so too.

10:26.355 --> 10:28.232
So, was the dive fun?

10:28.482 --> 10:29.108
Yes.

10:29.608 --> 10:30.901
That's good then.

10:31.110 --> 10:32.570
I was a bit worried at first.

10:32.736 --> 10:33.904
About what?

10:34.071 --> 10:36.448
Because you're serious but also clumsy,

10:36.740 --> 10:39.702
you didn't seem to be enjoying
yourself when diving for work.

10:40.953 --> 10:41.912
About that...

10:42.454 --> 10:46.292
If you want to make the customers happy,
you have to be happy yourself first.

10:46.876 --> 10:48.002
You're right.

10:48.377 --> 10:50.004
It's the same with relationships.

10:50.796 --> 10:52.923
If you want the other person to open up...

10:53.340 --> 10:55.467
You have to open up yourself.

10:55.634 --> 10:57.052
I'm glad you get it.

11:04.143 --> 11:05.186
What are you doing?

11:06.228 --> 11:07.605
Nothing.

11:07.730 --> 11:10.024
Oh, planning to apologize for yesterday?

11:10.191 --> 11:11.817
Then hurry up and go.

11:12.234 --> 11:12.902
But...

11:12.902 --> 11:13.819
It'll be fine.

11:14.111 --> 11:16.030
You're a lot like Sayaka-san.

11:17.323 --> 11:19.283
That mellow nature must be inherited.

11:19.283 --> 11:20.242
Be confident.

11:20.242 --> 11:22.077
That's quite rude, you know.

11:24.413 --> 11:25.414
I'm going.

11:25.414 --> 11:25.998
Oh.

11:26.207 --> 11:26.916
Good luck.

11:29.960 --> 11:31.837
So Mom...

11:32.546 --> 11:35.090
I want to apologize for yesterday.

11:35.758 --> 11:38.260
I know you're worried about me...

11:38.719 --> 11:42.097
but I still want to become
a diving instructor.

11:42.431 --> 11:46.268
I'll study and graduate
from college properly.

11:46.685 --> 11:49.980
Please let me try
being a diving instructor.

11:55.569 --> 11:57.154
What did you just say, Chisa?

11:59.031 --> 12:01.242
If you don't have any business, get out.

12:02.868 --> 12:04.620
I'm busy right now.

12:06.080 --> 12:09.041
GRAND BLUE DREAMING SEASON 3

12:15.214 --> 12:17.258
Isn't that a bit too harsh?

12:18.801 --> 12:20.844
Excuse me, I'm busy.

12:21.136 --> 12:22.429
Busy?

12:22.763 --> 12:25.307
You haven't seen her in ages,
how could you...

12:29.645 --> 12:31.730
Hello, this is Dolphin.

12:31.814 --> 12:32.982
Excuse me.

12:32.982 --> 12:36.360
This is Sugita from World Tour.
I want to ask about next week.

12:36.443 --> 12:38.654
Yes, who are you looking for?

12:38.654 --> 12:41.240
Excuse me, is Kotegawa-sama there?

12:41.323 --> 12:42.908
Please hold for a moment.

12:43.492 --> 12:44.201
Auntie.

12:44.451 --> 12:45.703
Bring it here to me.

12:47.788 --> 12:48.497
Here.

12:55.004 --> 12:57.214
What is it, more trouble?

12:58.215 --> 13:00.801
I don't understand what
you're saying. Speak slowly.

13:01.176 --> 13:02.303
Please talk more slowly.

13:03.554 --> 13:06.223
Iori, did something happen
with Chisa again?

13:06.307 --> 13:07.474
What do you mean?

13:07.641 --> 13:09.518
Because she's acting like that...

13:11.562 --> 13:12.688
She's smiling.

13:12.771 --> 13:13.731
She really is.

13:14.273 --> 13:17.818
How could Chisa have an expression
like that except when diving?

13:17.818 --> 13:20.237
You're saying some pretty harsh things.

13:20.821 --> 13:23.115
Maybe she's never been this mad before.

13:23.115 --> 13:24.199
Probably.

13:24.450 --> 13:26.201
She's that angry?

13:26.201 --> 13:28.203
If you don't believe it, try confirming it.

13:36.962 --> 13:38.380
Don't throw up, don't throw up.

13:39.256 --> 13:41.383
How angry must she be
for it to come to this?

13:41.383 --> 13:43.927
The pressure is so horrific
it makes you nauseous...

13:43.927 --> 13:45.179
What happened?

13:45.262 --> 13:47.348
Well, how should I put it?

13:47.890 --> 13:50.392
It seems to be the aftermath
of yesterday's events.

13:50.893 --> 13:51.935
Is that so?

13:51.935 --> 13:55.147
We shouldn't meddle in
other people's family matters.

13:55.397 --> 13:57.483
But today is our last day, right?

13:57.566 --> 14:00.611
There's almost no chance left
to resolve their conflict.

14:00.861 --> 14:02.529
What should we do?

14:02.654 --> 14:04.490
With those two's personalities...

14:04.656 --> 14:06.075
Hey, you three.

14:07.785 --> 14:08.619
Yes?

14:09.036 --> 14:10.537
Clean up the shop counter?

14:10.537 --> 14:13.749
No, I want to thank you
for working so hard.

14:14.541 --> 14:18.045
You can each pick an item
you like as a souvenir.

14:18.379 --> 14:19.213
Oh.

14:20.756 --> 14:22.049
What's wrong with him?

14:22.049 --> 14:23.550
I wonder what happened.

14:24.093 --> 14:26.136
You can't pick anything
too pricey, though.

14:26.345 --> 14:28.847
We should pick diving gear, right?

14:29.098 --> 14:31.100
A waterproof bag would be good too.

14:31.100 --> 14:33.394
There are a lot of things
we can't let get wet anyway.

14:33.560 --> 14:34.478
I see.

14:34.853 --> 14:36.271
I don't really need one.

14:36.271 --> 14:37.231
How about clothes?

14:38.482 --> 14:40.150
Looks like they have this too.

14:40.442 --> 14:42.069
Earplugs for divers?

14:42.694 --> 14:45.322
Using earplugs while diving is taboo.

14:45.572 --> 14:48.617
I heard water pressure pushes
earplugs deep inside.

14:48.617 --> 14:49.827
Ah, well...

14:50.077 --> 14:52.788
This type has tiny holes to...

14:52.788 --> 14:54.832
make equalizing ear pressure easier.

14:54.832 --> 14:55.791
Oh.

14:56.291 --> 14:58.961
Then Chisa probably wants
this more than I do.

14:59.545 --> 15:01.630
She had ear pain back
in Okinawa, after all.

15:01.839 --> 15:02.965
Now that you mention it.

15:03.799 --> 15:05.300
Have you picked anything?

15:05.717 --> 15:08.262
I'll take the waterproof bag.

15:08.345 --> 15:10.055
I still haven't decided.

15:10.180 --> 15:11.140
Is that so?

15:11.265 --> 15:15.561
Then how about the item a customer
left behind as a joke the other day?

15:15.561 --> 15:16.979
TROPICAL EROS

15:17.229 --> 15:18.272
Just kidding.

15:18.272 --> 15:20.524
How could that be a souvenir?

15:21.859 --> 15:24.111
I sincerely... thank you...

15:24.111 --> 15:25.070
Down to tears?

15:25.070 --> 15:27.072
He's that kind of guy.

15:29.616 --> 15:31.618
You'll certainly pick diving gear, right?

15:31.910 --> 15:32.661
No.

15:32.911 --> 15:34.621
I'll take this box of cookies.

15:34.746 --> 15:35.122
Huh?

15:35.247 --> 15:37.416
But that's not really a souvenir...

15:38.792 --> 15:39.751
It's fine.

15:40.085 --> 15:41.962
I don't need anything else.

15:44.715 --> 15:45.674
I see...

15:49.511 --> 15:51.889
Well then, you all worked hard.

15:52.389 --> 15:53.974
- Thank you both very much.
- Thank you both very much.

15:54.433 --> 15:56.810
Thanks for coming
even though the notice's short.

15:57.227 --> 16:00.105
The new hires are arriving
tomorrow, so no worries.

16:00.314 --> 16:02.232
We had a lot of fun too.

16:02.399 --> 16:02.983
Auntie...

16:03.150 --> 16:04.193
Where is the boss?

16:04.234 --> 16:06.278
She seems a bit busy.

16:06.361 --> 16:08.322
PAYCHECK
So she left this with me.

16:08.989 --> 16:09.823
Paychecks!

16:09.823 --> 16:11.158
Anime Blu-ray money!

16:11.366 --> 16:13.452
You've already planned what to do with it.

16:14.453 --> 16:16.872
Sorry it had to be paid in cash.

16:17.164 --> 16:18.290
No, it's totally fine.

16:19.374 --> 16:20.501
- Awesome!
- Alright.

16:20.501 --> 16:21.460
It's from the boss.

16:21.919 --> 16:22.711
Thank you.

16:23.670 --> 16:25.797
We should at least
say goodbye to the boss.

16:25.923 --> 16:26.632
Yeah.

16:27.799 --> 16:29.134
She looks busy.

16:29.676 --> 16:30.677
Yeah.

16:30.677 --> 16:32.137
Sorry about that.

16:32.596 --> 16:35.098
Goodbye, thank you four so much.

16:35.182 --> 16:36.475
It's our pleasure.

16:37.226 --> 16:39.019
- Thank you for taking care of us.
- Thank you for taking care of us.

16:41.980 --> 16:45.150
That's it, tomorrow
we just need to board the plane.

16:45.234 --> 16:47.819
It's great that we don't have to
wake up early tomorrow.

16:48.153 --> 16:49.071
In other words,

16:49.404 --> 16:52.324
tonight we can drink until we drop!

16:52.324 --> 16:54.701
We'd literally die!

16:54.952 --> 16:56.912
Chisa, say something too.

16:56.912 --> 16:57.871
That's right.

16:58.372 --> 16:59.581
Let's drink until we drop.

16:59.581 --> 17:00.707
Chisa?!

17:01.041 --> 17:03.210
I have to step in and stop them!

17:03.502 --> 17:05.212
Wait, hold on, Cakey.

17:05.295 --> 17:07.297
Just play along for now.

17:07.381 --> 17:08.298
Why?

17:08.382 --> 17:11.468
It's better to let her get drunk
and pour her heart out.

17:12.177 --> 17:14.221
Maybe, but...

17:14.596 --> 17:16.890
You absolutely cannot let
a disaster happen!

17:17.266 --> 17:19.226
Yeah, leave it to me.

17:23.438 --> 17:25.899
What... time is it?

17:27.192 --> 17:28.443
MS. AINA YOSHIWARA - PALAU TO NARITA
BOARDING TIME: 2:30 PM

17:28.610 --> 17:30.821
Everyone wake up!

17:32.990 --> 17:33.991
We made it!

17:34.616 --> 17:37.119
Actually, we still have plenty of time.

17:37.327 --> 17:40.747
You never know what might happen
at immigration control.

17:41.206 --> 17:42.541
What's wrong with you?

17:42.749 --> 17:44.418
Don't tell me you forgot something.

17:44.418 --> 17:45.043
Ah...

17:45.294 --> 17:47.921
Wallet, phone, keys,
how about your passport?

17:47.921 --> 17:48.589
Got them all.

17:48.589 --> 17:50.090
Then you're fine.

17:50.632 --> 17:52.509
It's not that. It's something else.

17:54.553 --> 17:55.637
Hello?

17:55.846 --> 17:57.848
Ah, Maki-san, what is it?

17:58.098 --> 18:00.100
You guys left something at the shop.

18:00.100 --> 18:00.517
Huh?

18:00.601 --> 18:02.060
What did we leave?

18:02.060 --> 18:02.603
Ah!

18:02.936 --> 18:04.855
The adult magazine I gave Iori-kun.

18:04.855 --> 18:05.981
TROPICAL EROS

18:05.981 --> 18:07.274
Ah...

18:07.816 --> 18:09.484
If that's it, then it's fine.

18:09.651 --> 18:11.987
Is that so? Got it, bye.

18:12.654 --> 18:13.196
Now then.

18:14.072 --> 18:15.657
Wait, where's Iori?

18:15.782 --> 18:17.451
If you mean Kitahara,

18:18.243 --> 18:19.578
-
That's it!
- he just yelled "That's it!"

18:19.578 --> 18:20.537
and dashed out.

18:20.871 --> 18:22.331
Huh?!

18:22.331 --> 18:24.541
Why didn't you stop him!?

18:25.000 --> 18:27.377
Because he looked
dead
serious.

18:27.669 --> 18:28.712
He's truly hopeless.

18:28.712 --> 18:29.713
That idiot.

18:30.172 --> 18:32.090
I-It'll probably be fine.

18:32.174 --> 18:36.345
Even Iori wouldn't miss his flight
just for an adult magazine...

18:38.221 --> 18:40.432
What a massive idiot!

18:43.894 --> 18:46.355
So Iori missed the flight.

18:46.813 --> 18:47.564
Yes.

18:47.898 --> 18:50.233
He ended up having to use
his part-time job money

18:50.233 --> 18:51.652
to buy a red-eye flight ticket.

18:51.777 --> 18:53.403
JAPAN / GUAM / PALAU
He likely has to layover in Guam.

18:53.570 --> 18:56.031
That must have cost quite a bit.

18:56.031 --> 18:58.659
What on earth
did he even come to Palau for?

18:59.785 --> 19:00.577
True that.

19:00.577 --> 19:03.121
Chisa-chan, did you talk to your mom?

19:05.040 --> 19:06.083
Chisa-chan?

19:06.291 --> 19:07.125
I have nothing...

19:07.626 --> 19:10.003
to say to that person.

19:10.754 --> 19:11.797
Chisa-chan...

19:24.184 --> 19:26.728
PAYCHECK

19:26.812 --> 19:28.146
I'm home, Chisa.

19:28.522 --> 19:30.023
Are you asleep already?

19:30.607 --> 19:32.734
If you're awake, just listen to me.

19:33.944 --> 19:37.239
Auntie ignored what
you said yesterday, right?

19:38.073 --> 19:40.200
That was a bit too much.

19:41.034 --> 19:41.910
It's fine.

19:42.327 --> 19:43.745
She's just one of those people.

19:44.121 --> 19:46.707
Well, I thought so too at first.

19:47.207 --> 19:49.334
But something didn't seem quite right.

19:49.876 --> 19:52.587
Auntie always cares about you.

19:53.630 --> 19:54.589
And then...

19:54.756 --> 19:57.384
seeing Cakey on the phone
made me remember.

19:58.301 --> 20:00.303
When I handed the phone to her,

20:00.679 --> 20:01.972
even though she was busy,

20:01.972 --> 20:04.182
she switched hands to hold the phone.

20:04.933 --> 20:06.184
What are you on about?

20:06.560 --> 20:08.395
You're being loud and annoying.

20:08.895 --> 20:10.522
Just hear me out.

20:11.231 --> 20:14.401
So when we got back to the shop,
I asked the manager.

20:15.819 --> 20:17.070
It turns out auntie...

20:18.363 --> 20:20.407
is deaf in her left ear.

20:23.535 --> 20:24.286
Huh?

20:25.412 --> 20:28.331
I heard she used to be
a diving instructor.

20:29.916 --> 20:33.211
Even for instructors, there are times
when they can't equalize ear pressure.

20:33.712 --> 20:35.922
Do you know what they should do
at times like that?

20:36.173 --> 20:38.008
The only choice is to surface, right?

20:38.425 --> 20:40.677
That's what they should do.

20:41.887 --> 20:43.889
But they often endure it to keep diving.

20:44.973 --> 20:48.602
Doing that repeatedly must've
damaged her eardrum.

20:49.311 --> 20:50.479
No way.

20:51.104 --> 20:52.731
I had no idea...

20:52.939 --> 20:55.817
If she couldn't hear,
she could've just told me.

20:56.359 --> 20:58.278
She probably found it hard to say.

20:59.279 --> 21:02.032
Because the main cause was diving,
which you love so much.

21:03.033 --> 21:05.202
You two really are very alike.

21:05.410 --> 21:07.579
From worrying about your ears...

21:07.996 --> 21:10.791
To being clumsy in expressing
your feelings...

21:11.458 --> 21:13.251
PAYCHECK

21:15.462 --> 21:17.923
DO YOUR BEST

21:26.515 --> 21:27.557
Mom.

21:32.437 --> 21:33.772
Well then, good night.

21:34.356 --> 21:35.982
Yeah, good night.

21:44.491 --> 21:45.283
What is it?

21:46.284 --> 21:48.370
Before sleeping, I want to ask one thing.

21:48.787 --> 21:49.704
Could it be...

21:49.996 --> 21:53.124
you missed your flight because of me?

21:53.750 --> 21:56.586
I forgot my adult magazine anyway.

21:57.504 --> 21:58.421
I see.

21:58.880 --> 22:00.382
Thank you, Iori.

22:00.632 --> 22:03.260
Jeez, why are you being so honest
all of a sudden?

22:03.343 --> 22:05.595
Yeah, I wanted to say it honestly.

22:06.555 --> 22:10.016
I'm really glad I have you.

22:19.651 --> 22:21.278
3... 2... 1... Go!

22:30.829 --> 22:33.582
A sweet little love story!?

22:33.582 --> 22:36.334
Asymmetrical reflection in the mirror

22:36.334 --> 22:37.961
A shattered, crunchy heart

22:37.961 --> 22:40.005
Oh oh, stumbling around

22:40.589 --> 22:43.008
Oh oh, just acting on instinct

22:43.008 --> 22:46.970
Diving deep into my subconscious

22:46.970 --> 22:48.722
Tumbling and falling down

22:48.722 --> 22:51.308
A limit-breaking paradise

22:51.308 --> 22:52.559
Viva, cheers

22:52.559 --> 22:54.019
Everyone, cheers

22:54.019 --> 22:56.062
We're in trouble, we're in trouble

22:56.062 --> 22:56.771
Big trouble

22:56.771 --> 22:58.773
We're in trouble, we're in trouble

22:58.773 --> 22:59.608
Wa wa wa

22:59.608 --> 23:01.568
We're in trouble, we're in trouble

23:01.568 --> 23:02.277
Wa wa wa wa

23:02.277 --> 23:04.237
Let's go, everybody

23:04.237 --> 23:07.699
Dramatic just like a rainbow

23:07.699 --> 23:10.702
Your troubled smile
is absolutely priceless

23:10.702 --> 23:15.999
Total chaos
getting kissed by an octopus

23:15.999 --> 23:18.752
A mermaid washed up on the shore

23:18.752 --> 23:21.671
Darling drowned down
in the Dragon Palace

23:21.671 --> 23:26.968
The treasure box is just full of alcohol

23:26.968 --> 23:29.679
The ultimate license of our youth

23:29.679 --> 23:32.641
Find the treasure and checkmate

23:32.641 --> 23:37.854
An angel who overslept
from swimming too much

23:37.854 --> 23:39.314
Let's go, everybody

23:39.314 --> 23:40.690
Viva, cheers

23:40.690 --> 23:42.025
Oh yeah

23:42.025 --> 23:43.693
Viva, cheers
